@startuml BC-08_Subscription

note as ImplementationNote
  Subscription is infrastructure + presentation only — there
  is no domain.model or resource/assembler layer. SubscriptionApi
  returns the backend's raw JSON straight through, and the
  views consume it directly (e.g. plan.id, plan.name, plan.price,
  plan.tier fields read directly off the plain response objects).
end note

package "subscription.infrastructure" {
  class SubscriptionApi {
    + constructor()
    + getPlans(): Promise<object[]>
    + getMySubscription(): Promise<{hasActiveSubscription, status, subscription}>
    + confirmCheckout(sessionId: string): Promise<{active: boolean}>
    + createCheckoutSession(planId, planName, amount): Promise<{checkoutUrl: string}>
  }
}

package "subscription.presentation.views" {
  class SelectPlanView <<view>> {
    - plans: Ref<object[]>
    - period: Ref<"monthly" | "yearly">
    - loadingPlans: Ref<boolean>
    - checkingOutPlanId: Ref<number | null>
    - confirmingPayment: Ref<boolean>
    - error: Ref<string | null>
    - visiblePlans: ComputedRef<object[]>
    - hasYearlyPlans: ComputedRef<boolean>
    + monthlyPrice(plan): string
    + confirmPaymentReturn(): Promise<void>
    + selectPlan(plan): Promise<void>
  }
  class PaymentSuccessView <<view>> {
    - state: Ref<"confirming" | "success" | "error">
    + confirm(): Promise<void>
  }
}

package "subscription.presentation" {
  class SubscriptionRoutes <<configuration>> {
    + "/select-plan"     -> SelectPlanView
    + "/payment-success" -> PaymentSuccessView
  }
}

BaseApi <|-- SubscriptionApi

SelectPlanView --> SubscriptionApi : uses (getPlans, createCheckoutSession)
SelectPlanView --> AuthStore : uses (refreshSubscription)
PaymentSuccessView --> SubscriptionApi : uses (confirmCheckout)
PaymentSuccessView --> AuthStore : uses (setSubscriptionActive, logout)

note right of SelectPlanView
  Plans are grouped into monthly/yearly by matching a regex
  against plan.name ("Mensual" vs "Anual") rather than a
  dedicated field, then sorted cheapest-first. Yearly plans
  store the FULL annual price; monthlyPrice() divides by 12
  for display only.

  On return from Stripe (?status=success), polls
  authStore.refreshSubscription() up to 6 times (1.5s apart)
  waiting for the webhook/return handler to activate the
  subscription before redirecting to /panel.
end note

note right of PaymentSuccessView
  Polls SubscriptionApi.confirmCheckout(sessionId) up to 5
  times. On success, redirects to /login if the purchase came
  from the registration funnel (sessionStorage flag
  "postPurchaseRedirect"), otherwise straight to /panel.
end note

note right of SubscriptionApi
  createCheckoutSession's response is either a real absolute
  Stripe Checkout URL (redirect the browser to pay) or a
  relative app path (local dev-activate — already active,
  no real payment involved).
end note

@enduml
